 - parse input
	q
		quit no output
	p <ean> <iva> <price> <amount> <desc>
		new product. outputs stock
		errors: invalid ean invalid iva invalid price invalid quantify invalid desc.
			product in use invalid product 
	l [ wildcard ]
		list avaliable. outputs ean iva price sold avaliable desc
		ordered by arg and criation order
		wildcards: * and ? represent any caracter possible or sequence
		errors: wildcard no such product
	a [[amount] ean]
		add to basket the amount specified. outputs iva price amount totalw iva desc
		basket is initially empty
		if no amount, assume 1
		when added or removed, always list, no matter the result
		if no aarcs, print the list order by ean, no doubles, no null
		errors: invalid ean invalid amount no such product no stock
	r [ean]
		summary of invoices and existence. outputs avaliable sold desc if argument,
		total bought, total invoices emited total amount earned
		errors: invalid ean no such product 
	f [[nif] name] 
		invoice the basket. if no nif 999999999. if no name, "Cliente final". if name
		is error, return items and dont print.
		invoice numbers do not repear, are sequencial starting at one and go on even 
		if one is deleted
		if without errors, empty basket
		errors: no such nif invalid name
	d <number> [amount]
		delete product or invoice. outputs value nif cllient if only has one arg and
		the invoice is deleted but items arent restocked. if two args, output amount desc
		and amount is removed from available. if nothing left, remove from registered.
		errors: no such invoice invalid ean no such product product in use 
			invalid quantity
	c [name]
		list invoices for a client. outputs number value name if no args. print by 
		alphabetical order and chronological per client. if arg, only chronological
		errors: invalid name no such client
 - handle barcodes
	ean 13
	ean 8
	for both:  sum the even, sub 3*odd for each odd and do 10-(sum%10)%10 for last digit
 - description of products
	start with capital letter
	up to 50 bytes
 - invoices
	amount of items and values
	nif number with 9 digits
	name of client: may have blank spaces or \t, if it does, "name", if not, can also be
			no max length, shouldnt excede 50 bytes
			may start with capital or not
	up to 10000 per instance
	no limit of products per invoice
	no limit of receits
	no limit for client name
 - no more than 65535 chars (64k bytes)
 - if exceeds, control the exit and print "No memory."
 - free all memory before exiting
 - should be able to call it with a file of codes and iva values
	one entry per line: capital letter and int (% iva)
	if no file, use A 0, B 6, C 13, D 23
	can have up to 26 codes non consecutive
 - cents are rounded simetrically	
				

 - dont use goto, extern or qsort, dont even have it in your code. 
 - may use stdio.h, stdlib.h, ctypy.h and string.h
 - compile with gcc -03 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Wno-unused-result
 - use tabs, not spaces. no more than 80 chars per line.
 - curly brackers same line as header and end bracket aligned with the header for functions, if, 	
	while, switch and for.
 - comment using doxygen format. each file should hae author name and summary. each function should
 - have comment with summary. each global or static should have a why in the same line or line 
	before
